s.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-10/age1102.pdf)\nciteturn1694search14 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Order Granting Attorney’s Motion to be Relieved as Counsel—Civil (revise form MC-053) (Action Required) ... The Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee recommends adopting four new forms to provide parties and the court with direction for completing all steps necessary to enter an unlawful detainer (a) judgment, (b) conditional judgment (c) stipulation for entry of judgment, and (d) declaration for default and judgment by the court.\nItem A13\n\nOrder Granting Attorney’s Motion to be Relieved as Counsel—Civil (revise form MC-053) (Action Required)\n\nStaff: Mr. Patrick O’Donnell\n\nThe Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee recommends revising a form order to include a provision indicating where the client must be served after the motion to be relieved as counsel is granted.\n\nItem A14\n\nPretrial Rules (amend Cal. Rules of Court, rules 313, 321, and 323; repeal rule 377) (Action Required)\n\nStaff: Mr. Patrick O’Donnell\n\nThe Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee recommends amending rules on law and motion hearings to be clearer and consistent with the policy favoring the use of plain language. The committee further recommends repealing a rule on advisory juries that is no longer necessary.\n\nItem A15\n\nUnlawful Detainer Judgment Forms (approve forms UD-110, UD-110S, UD-115, and UD-116) (Action Required)\n\nStaff: Ms. Cara Vonk\n\nThe Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee recommends adopting four new forms to provide parties and the court with direction for completing all steps necessary to enter an unlawful detainer (a) judgment, (b) conditional judgment (c) stipulation for entry of judgment, and (d) declaration for default and judgment by the court.\n\nItem A16\n\nAuthorization to Appear on Behalf of Party (Small Claims) (approve form SC-109) (Action Required)\n\nStaff: Ms. Cara Vonk--------------------------------------